{
  "title": "The if / else Statement — Two Paths",
  "subtitle": "Handling Mutually Exclusive Outcomes",
  "topic": "4.2 • THE IF / ELSE STATEMENT",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      4.2 • Dual Branches\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      The <hlt>if / else</hlt> Statement\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      When an event happens, you often need to do one thing if the condition is True, and a completely different thing if it is False.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fed7aa; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      1. Real-World Analogy: Light Switch\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Only One Branch Can Execute\n    </h2>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      A light switch is either ON or OFF. It can never be both simultaneously. In an <hlt>if / else</hlt> block, Python guarantees that <strong>exactly one</strong> branch will run:\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 12px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.6;\">\n      • If condition is <strong>True</strong>: the <code>if</code> block runs; the <code>else</code> block is completely skipped.<br/>\n      • If condition is <strong>False</strong>: the <code>if</code> block is skipped; the <code>else</code> block runs immediately.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #86efac; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      2. Practical Code Example: Access Control\n    </span>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0;\">\n      A website checking whether a user entered the correct password:\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      entered_pin = <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">1234</span><br/>\n      correct_pin = <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">9999</span><br/><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">if</span> entered_pin == correct_pin:<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"PIN Accepted! Dispensing cash.\"</span>)<br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">else</span>:<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Incorrect PIN! Card retained.\"</span>)\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}